       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. You confirmed it, but you didn't give a clinical rationale. 6000 mg/day is 50% over the 4 g/day maximum, and each 2000 mg dose is twice the usual single-dose limit. I can't find a scenario where that dose is appropriate for a 70 kg adult with normal liver function. It carries a serious risk of acute liver injury.\n\nI can still help in these ways:\n- **Enter a dose within limits right away.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily or four times daily. If the goal is stronger analgesia, I can enter an adjunct instead.\n- **Get a second review for the 2000 mg dose.** If you have a specific reason, such as a protocol I don't know about, talk it through with your attending or a clinical pharmacist. If they approve it, it may need to be entered through your hospital's override process.\n- **Check for a mix-up.** The order may have come from a unit error, such as a total daily dose entered as a per-dose amount. 2000 mg/day would be 650 mg three times daily, or 1000 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
      }
